# Keep the build context small and the image free of anything host-specific.
#
# Two entries here are load-bearing rather than housekeeping:
#   .env*        secrets must never be baked into a layer, and Next would otherwise
#                read them at build time and inline NEXT_PUBLIC_* values from a
#                developer's laptop into the production bundle.
#   src/generated  the Prisma client is regenerated inside the builder. Copying a
#                  host-generated copy risks shipping one built from a stale schema.

node_modules
.next
out
build

.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

src/generated
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# Local-only tooling and docs. Nothing here affects the build.
.claude
.vscode
.idea
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
npm-debug.log*

# Credentials the GitHub auth action writes into the workspace. `builds submit`
# uploads the whole directory, so without this the file goes to Cloud Build.
gha-creds-*.json
